---
import Reading from '../../../layouts/Reading.astro';
import ProjectList from '../../../components/ProjectList.astro';
import { projectsOfKind } from '../../../data/projects';

const startups = projectsOfKind('startup');
---
<Reading
  title="Startups — Kevin Holler"
  description="The three companies Kevin Holler has started: Shake, Trackplan, and Suky."
  here="startups"
>
  <h1>Startups</h1>
  <p class="stamp">Three companies. Two of them are over.</p>

  <p class="lede">
    Shake, Trackplan, Suky — in reverse order, which is also the order in
    which I knew what I was doing. Each has a page with what it was, what
    happened, and what I took from it.
  </p>

  <p>
    Two of the three did not work, and both of those pages say so at the top
    rather than in a paragraph near the bottom. When my first company failed I
    wrote the shutdown post publicly, and what came back — job offers,
    interview requests, founders emailing to say the same thing had happened
    to them — taught me that the thing I was most afraid to say out loud was
    the thing other people most needed to hear. That is still the standard
    these pages are held to.
  </p>

  <ProjectList entries={startups} />
</Reading>
